# FlatMate OS: End-User Experience & Frontend Implementation Plan

This plan is focused purely on the **end-user perspective**, **visual design**, and **frontend client implementation**. It outlines what flatmates see on their phones and desktops, how they interact with each screen, and how GitHub Copilot will build the React components.

---

## 1. End-User Journey & Screen Flow

Flatmates interact with the app via four intuitive tabs in a mobile-first Progressive Web App (PWA) layout:

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      SCREEN FLOW                       │
├───────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┤
│ View              │ Primary User Goal                  │
├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 1. Smart Buy List │ At store/Zepto: See what is out    │
│                   │ of stock; tap "Bought It".         │
├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 2. Kitchen Pantry │ In flat: 1-tap toggles to mark     │
│                   │ items In Stock, Low, or Empty.     │
├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 3. Expense Ledger │ Track who paid what, view house    │
│                   │ budget burn progress, log bills.   │
├───────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 4. Settlement Hub │ Month-end: Tap "Pay via UPI" to    │
│                   │ settle flat debts with zero math.  │
└───────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┘

```

